<div data-controller="profile-mcp" data-profile-mcp-profile-url-value="{{ path('profile_show') }}" data-profile-mcp-endpoint-value="/mcp/compose" data-profile-mcp-expected-resource-value="{{ connection.endpoint }}" data-profile-mcp-expected-issuer-value="{{ connection.issuer }}" class="space-y-8 min-w-0">
<section id="mcp" aria-labelledby="mcp-title" class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100"><div class="card-body min-w-0">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3"><h2 id="mcp-title" class="card-title">MCP connections</h2><span class="badge {{ connection.enabled ? 'badge-success' : 'badge-warning' }}">{{ connection.enabled ? 'Server enabled' : 'Server disabled' }}</span></div>
    <p>Create a personal credential to let Codex create and edit catalogue compositions with your permissions.</p>
    <p class="text-sm break-all"><span class="font-medium">Server URL:</span> <span data-profile-mcp-target="endpoint">{{ connection.endpoint }}</span> <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs" data-action="profile-mcp#copy" data-profile-mcp-source-param="endpoint">Copy URL</button></p>
    {% if not connection.enabled %}<p role="status" class="alert alert-warning">This deployment has MCP disabled. Your deployment administrator must enable it before a client can connect. You can prepare credentials and configuration here.</p>{% endif %}
    {% if is_granted('ROLE_EDITOR') %}
    {% if plain %}<p role="status" class="alert alert-success" data-new-mcp-secret>Credential created. Its secret is available below only on this page. Copy it before leaving.</p>{% endif %}
    <details class="collapse collapse-arrow border border-base-300 mt-4" {% if errorSection == 'mcp' %}open{% endif %}><summary class="collapse-title font-semibold">Create a personal MCP credential</summary><div class="collapse-content">
        <form action="{{ path('profile_mcp_token_create') }}" method="post" data-turbo="false" class="grid gap-4">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('profile-mcp') }}">
            <div class="grid gap-2"><label for="mcp-label" class="font-medium">Credential name</label><input id="mcp-label" name="label" value="{{ tokenValues.label }}" class="input w-full" required maxlength="100"></div>
            <fieldset class="fieldset"><legend class="fieldset-legend">Composer permissions</legend>{% for scope,label in scopeLabels %}<label class="label whitespace-normal"><input type="checkbox" name="scopes[]" value="{{ scope }}" class="checkbox checkbox-sm" {% if scope in tokenValues.scopes %}checked{% endif %}>{{ label }}</label>{% endfor %}<p class="text-sm opacity-70">Read access is needed for discovery and editing. No permission grants source authoring or publishing.</p></fieldset>
            <div class="grid gap-2"><label for="mcp-patterns" class="font-medium">Catalogue access</label><textarea id="mcp-patterns" name="patterns" class="textarea w-full font-mono" rows="2" maxlength="2000" required aria-describedby="mcp-patterns-help">{{ tokenValues.patterns }}</textarea><p id="mcp-patterns-help" class="text-sm opacity-70">Use * for all accessible catalogue items, or namespace/* and namespace/slug, separated by spaces or commas. Include referenced dependencies.</p></div>
            <div class="grid gap-2"><label for="mcp-days" class="font-medium">Expires in days</label><input id="mcp-days" type="number" name="days" value="{{ tokenValues.days }}" class="input w-full" required min="1" max="90"></div>
            <div><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create MCP credential</button></div>
        </form>
    </div></details>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3" id="mcp-test">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Test this connection</h3><p class="text-sm opacity-70">The browser authenticates against this server, discovers the tools and calls read-only composer capabilities. Your catalogue stays unchanged.</p>
        <label for="mcp-bearer" class="font-medium">MCP bearer token</label><input id="mcp-bearer" type="password" class="input w-full font-mono" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" maxlength="2048" value="{{ plain|default('') }}" placeholder="Paste your personal MCP token" data-profile-mcp-target="credential">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="profile-mcp#test" data-profile-mcp-target="runButton">Test MCP connection</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" data-action="profile-mcp#copy" data-profile-mcp-source-param="credential">Copy token</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" data-action="profile-mcp#reveal" data-profile-mcp-source-param="credential" aria-pressed="false">Show token</button></div>
        <p role="status" aria-live="polite" data-profile-mcp-target="result">No browser connection test has run.</p><ul hidden class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm" data-profile-mcp-target="checks"></ul>
    </div>
    <details class="collapse collapse-arrow border border-base-300 mt-4"><summary class="collapse-title font-semibold">Connect Codex</summary><div class="collapse-content min-w-0 space-y-4">
        <p>Merge this into your Codex configuration. Set <code class="break-all">STYLEGUIDE_COMPOSE_MCP_TOKEN</code> in the environment of the Codex app, IDE or CLI, then restart its connection.</p>
        <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-all rounded-box bg-base-200 p-4 text-sm" data-profile-mcp-target="config"><code>{{ connection.toml }}</code></pre>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" data-action="profile-mcp#copy" data-profile-mcp-source-param="config">Copy Codex configuration</button><a class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" href="{{ path('profile_mcp_codex') }}" data-turbo="false">Download Codex configuration</a></div>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-70">The configuration contains an environment reference. Store your token in private client settings. A browser check verifies this server; Codex must also reach the URL from its own computer or container.</p>
        <a class="link" href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp?surface=cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official Codex MCP instructions</a>
    </div></details>
    <div class="mt-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Your credentials</h3><p class="mb-3 text-sm opacity-70">Secrets are stored as hashes and cannot be displayed again. Revocation takes effect on the next request.</p>
    <ul class="space-y-3" data-mcp-credentials>{% for credential in credentials %}<li class="rounded-box border border-base-300 p-4" data-credential-id="{{ credential.id }}"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3"><div class="min-w-0"><p class="font-semibold break-all">{{ credential.label }}</p><p class="text-sm">Created {{ credential.createdAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }} · Expires {{ credential.expiresAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }} UTC</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm break-all">{{ credential.scopes|join(', ') }}</p><p class="font-mono text-sm break-all">{{ credential.cataloguePatterns|join(', ') }}</p></div>{% if credential.active %}<form action="{{ path('profile_mcp_token_revoke',{id:credential.id}) }}" method="post" data-turbo="false"><input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('profile-mcp') }}"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Revoke {{ credential.label }}</button></form>{% else %}<span class="badge badge-ghost">{{ credential.revokedAt ? 'Revoked' : 'Expired' }}</span>{% endif %}</div></li>{% else %}<li class="text-sm opacity-70">No personal MCP credentials yet.</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
    {% else %}<p class="alert alert-info mt-4">Your account has read-only studio access. MCP composition connections require an editor or administrator role.</p>{% endif %}
</div></section>
<section id="chatgpt" aria-labelledby="chatgpt-title" class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100"><div class="card-body min-w-0">
    <h2 id="chatgpt-title" class="card-title">ChatGPT OAuth setup</h2><p>ChatGPT uses OAuth account linking. Add the server in ChatGPT Plugins → + → Add custom MCP server, choose OAuth and copy its exact callback URL.</p>
    <p class="text-sm {{ connection.publicHttps ? '' : 'text-warning' }}">{{ connection.publicHttps ? 'An HTTPS URL is configured. ChatGPT still needs network access to the server and authorization pages.' : 'This is a local HTTP deployment. A ChatGPT connection needs reachable HTTPS or a supported Secure MCP Tunnel arrangement, including access to the login pages.' }}</p>
    <div class="my-3"><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" type="button" data-action="profile-mcp#testOauth">Check OAuth server setup</button></div><p role="status" aria-live="polite" data-profile-mcp-target="oauthResult">ChatGPT account linking has not been verified here.</p>
    {% if is_granted('ROLE_ADMIN') %}
        {% if newClient %}<div class="alert alert-success my-4"><div class="w-full min-w-0 space-y-3"><p class="font-semibold">OAuth client created. Copy its secret into your ChatGPT connection now; it will not be shown again.</p><label for="oauth-client-id">Client ID</label><input id="oauth-client-id" class="input w-full font-mono" readonly value="{{ newClient.id }}" data-profile-mcp-target="clientId"><label for="oauth-client-secret">Client secret</label><input id="oauth-client-secret" class="input w-full font-mono" type="password" readonly value="{{ newClient.secret }}" autocomplete="off" data-profile-mcp-target="clientSecret"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button class="btn btn-sm" type="button" data-action="profile-mcp#copy" data-profile-mcp-source-param="clientId">Copy client ID</button><button class="btn btn-sm" type="button" data-action="profile-mcp#copy" data-profile-mcp-source-param="clientSecret">Copy client secret</button></div></div></div>{% endif %}
        <details class="collapse collapse-arrow border border-base-300" {% if errorSection == 'oauth' %}open{% endif %}><summary class="collapse-title font-semibold">Register a ChatGPT OAuth client</summary><div class="collapse-content">
            <form action="{{ path('profile_mcp_oauth_create') }}" method="post" data-turbo="false" class="grid gap-4"><input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('profile-oauth') }}">
            <div class="grid gap-2"><label for="oauth-label" class="font-medium">OAuth client name</label><input id="oauth-label" name="label" class="input w-full" required maxlength="100" value="{{ oauthValues.label }}"></div>
            <div class="grid gap-2"><label for="oauth-redirect" class="font-medium">Exact ChatGPT callback URL</label><input id="oauth-redirect" name="redirect" type="url" class="input w-full" required maxlength="300" value="{{ oauthValues.redirect }}" placeholder="https://chatgpt.com/connector_platform_oauth_redirect"><p class="text-sm opacity-70">Use the URL shown by your ChatGPT connection. Registration requires authorization code, S256 PKCE and the four composer scopes.</p></div>
            <div><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create OAuth client</button></div></form>
        </div></details>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">{% for client in oauthClients %}<li class="rounded-box border border-base-300 p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3"><div class="min-w-0"><p class="font-semibold break-all">{{ client.name }}</p><code class="text-sm break-all">{{ client.identifier }}</code>{% for redirect in client.redirectUris %}<p class="text-sm break-all">{{ redirect }}</p>{% endfor %}</div>{% if client.active %}<form action="{{ path('profile_mcp_oauth_disable',{id:client.identifier}) }}" method="post" data-turbo="false"><input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('profile-oauth') }}"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Disable {{ client.name }}</button></form>{% else %}<form action="{{ path('profile_mcp_oauth_enable',{id:client.identifier}) }}" method="post" data-turbo="false"><input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('profile-oauth') }}"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Enable {{ client.name }}</button></form>{% endif %}</div></li>{% else %}<li class="text-sm opacity-70">No predefined OAuth clients.</li>{% endfor %}</ul><p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">These administrator settings are shared. Disabling a client disconnects every account linked through it.</p>
    {% else %}<p class="my-3 text-sm opacity-70">A studio administrator can register your callback URL from their profile and provide the OAuth client details.</p>{% endif %}
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm">Finish linking in ChatGPT, sign in to the studio and approve the composer scopes. Select the connection in a new conversation and call composer capabilities. This page checks local server readiness; only a successful call from ChatGPT verifies that account connection.</p>
    <a class="link mt-2" href="https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official ChatGPT connection instructions</a>
</div></section>
<p role="status" aria-live="polite" data-profile-mcp-target="feedback"></p>
</div>
